  "notes": [
    "Research pass of 2026-11-17 (Task RB-BIO). All sources were fetched live in this pass; every URL recorded below was actually retrieved and read.",
    "neet-ug: register uses the NMC/UGMEB 'Updated syllabus for NEET (UG)-2026' notice (dated 2025-12-22, hosted on nta.ac.in). Lines = the 10 stated NEET Biology units plus the current rationalised NCERT Class 11+12 chapter titles the syllabus covers (per ledger granularity rule: chapter-level lines, sub-bullet detail not exploded). NEET 2026 retains no 'Digestion and Absorption', 'Transport in Plants', 'Mineral Nutrition', 'Reproduction in Organisms', 'Strategies for Enhancement in Food Production' or 'Environmental Issues' (rationalised scope).",
    "ncert-biology-11/12: ncert.nic.in itself is unreachable from this sandbox (DNS fails and a --resolve attempt to its NIC IP also fails), so the CURRENT rationalised chapter lists were taken from the official CBSE Senior Secondary Curriculum 2026-27, Biology (044) PDF on cbseacademic.nic.in, which lists the chapter set of the current NCERT rationalised textbooks: Class XI = 19 chapters (The Living World retained; Transport in Plants and Mineral Nutrition remain deleted), Class XII = 13 chapters (Reproduction in Organisms, Strategies for Enhancement in Food Production and Environmental Issues remain deleted). This matches the NEET 2026 notice's unit content.",
    "CBSE 2026-27 additionally teaches 'Digestion and Absorption' (Class XI) and 'Environmental Issues' (Class XII) as formative-only CBSE Reading Material (not NCERT chapters); these are excluded from the chapter lines and only noted here for honesty.",
    "cuet-ug: the official CUET (UG) 2026 Biology/Biological Science/Biotechnology/Biochemistry (304) syllabus PDF contains Units VI-X only (Class 12 NCERT-aligned) - this is NTA's 2026 domain-subject scope, not an extraction gap; corroborated by the official CUET 2026 Chemistry PDF which likewise covers only Class-12 units. Units I-V (Class 11) are not part of CUET UG 2026 Biology.",
    "gate-xl: the official GATE 2026 mapping (IIT Guwahati PDFs, fetched and read) is XL-P = Chemistry (compulsory for all XL candidates), XL-Q = Biochemistry, XL-R = Botany, XL-S = Microbiology, XL-T = Zoology, XL-U = Food Technology. The task brief's parentheticals (P=Biotechnology, Q=Botany, R=Zoology, S=Biochemistry, T=Microbiology) do not match any official GATE XL mapping - GATE Biotechnology is the separate BT paper. The official letters and content were used; XL-P's nine chemistry sub-sections are recorded as officially stated (cross-discipline content, for routing by the owning chemistry shelf).",
    "gate-xl General Aptitude (GA) lines are excluded for every GATE entry per ledger convention (GA is common to all GATE papers and is not biology content).",
    "gate-xl-q (Biochemistry): its six sub-sections are UNTITLED in the official PDF ('Section 1'...'Section 6' only), so its lines are the named topics as stated within each section (leading semicolon-separated clauses; post-colon illustrative detail skipped per granularity rule).",
    "gate-xl-u (Food Technology): the official PDF text ends mid-sentence inside Section 4 (Food Engineering) on the IIT Guwahati site - verified identical in both the per-section and combined XL PDFs; the four section titles are unaffected.",
    "ib-biology: ibo.org returns 403 from this sandbox, so the topic structure of the current IB Biology guide (2023 guide, first exams 2025) was verified through two independent reputable mirrors (BioNinja and Save My Exams). Mirror naming variants exist: Save My Exams' 'Protein Synthesis' folder = guide subtopics D2 Transcription + D3 Translation; 'Natural Selection' = guide's D11 Selection; 'Cell & Nuclear Division' = D5 Cell division. The guide form is used here. The Tools and Inquiry-process sections are included as syllabus structure lines.",
    "a-levels-biology: Cambridge 9700 syllabus for exams 2025-2027 used (current, official PDF). The 2028-2030 syllabus PDF was also fetched and checked: identical 19-topic structure. 'Practical skills' is added as the syllabus's stated practical component line (AS and A Level).",
    "ibo: the IBO's permanent association site ibo-info.org is unreachable from this sandbox and its predecessor domain ibo-official.org no longer resolves at all (NXDOMAIN via DoH). The current host's official site ibo2026.lt (37th IBO, Vilnius, July 2026) publishes the current stated syllabus structure: 7 theory areas with proportions and 4 practical exam areas; theory-area names corroborated by Wikipedia's archived description (2009 revision). Proportions (Cell biology 20%, Plant anatomy and physiology 15%, Animal anatomy and physiology 25%, Ethology 5%, Genetics and Evolution 20%, Ecology 10%, Biosystematics 5%) are recorded here because the topic lines carry bare names.",
    "ap-biology: units 1-8 exactly as the official College Board course pages state them.",
    "Dedupe note: where a unit title and a chapter title are identical in the official syllabus (Unit IX / Chapter 'Biotechnology and its Applications' in NCERT Class 12, CUET and NEET), the line is recorded once under the unit title - an identical chapter line adds no coverage. The NEET unit is officially titled 'Biotechnology and Its Applications' (capital Its in the notice).",
    "Line census of this file: 276 total = neet-ug 41, ncert-biology-11 24, ncert-biology-12 17, cuet-ug 17, gate-xl-p 9, gate-xl-q 40, gate-xl-r 9, gate-xl-s 11, gate-xl-t 11, gate-xl-u 4, ap-biology 8, ib-biology 51, a-levels-biology 20, ibo 14."
